BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:E Pluribus Unum (Out of Many\, One): 400 Years of American Song
DTSTART:20261122T160000
DTEND:20261122T180000
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:a1d910e9a424ee0870c0107ed7a1f9@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Vermont Choral Union (VCU) announces its new music directo
 r\, Cole Marino. This is Cole's fourth season with VCU\, having spent the 
 previous three in the bass section and as assistant director. A Vermont na
 tive\, Cole has a deep love for music in all its forms and is passionate a
 bout bringing musicians and audiences together for adventurous and vibrant
  performances. Under Cole’s direction\, VCU is very excited to present a
  selection of American music\, highlighting the works of Aaron Copland alo
 ngside other\, lesser-known composers including Amy Beach\, Samuel Barber
 \, Harry Burleigh\, and Queen Liliʻuokalani\, the last reigning monarch o
 f Hawaiʻi. The program explores the questions posed by American identity
 \, and highlights the conflicting experiences of grief\, joy\, humor\, and
  pride that come with it. The program will be accompanied by spoken word r
 eflections selected and performed by local high-school students. These spo
 ken interludes\, quotes from notable Americans on a range of subjects\, wi
 ll serve to place the music in a new context\, and shape the evening in a 
 unique and meaningful way. Promising an evening of music that delights\, c
 hallenges\, and entertains\, this is a performance you won’t want to mis
 s! Featuring: Len Torrie (soprano\, Montreal)\, Ryan Matos (tenor\, Burlin
 gton)\, Cole Marino (baritone\, Williston)\, Eric Milnes (piano\, organ)\,
  Peter Berton (organ\, piano)\, and a group of local high school students 
 - names TBA (speakers) Performance Schedule 21 November 2026 22 November 2
 026\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:College Street Congregational Church\, 265 College Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/e-pluribus
 -unum-out-of-many-one-400-years-of-american-song-09-11-2026-17-02-05
END:VEVENT
