BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jesse Peters\, Ezra Holloway\, and George Nostrand at Stage 33 Liv
 e
DTSTART:20261122T190000
DTEND:20261122T203000
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:f18f01adaf292b52b54051fa1efd2d@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Another In the ongoing Local Curator series at Stage 33 Live\,
  three Southern Vermont music scene mainstays on one bill: Jesse Peters\, 
 Ezra Holloway\, and George Nostrand in an acoustic round-robin show on Sun
 day\, November 22\, 7:00 at Stage 33 Live. 33 Bridge Street in Bellows Fal
 ls\, Vermont. Tickets are a discounted $10 in advance through stage33live.
 com\, or $15 at the door as available. Advance tickets guarantee entry. On
 ly 40 tickets will be sold. All ticket money goes to the performers. More 
 info at the stage33live.com website. Jesse Peters is eclectic in his taste
 s and writing — he graduated The University of The Arts in Philadelphia 
 with a bachelor’s in jazz guitar\, playing acoustic music in coffee hous
 es along the way. He remains committed to a mix of styles while remaining 
 focused and accessible. A strong writer and top-notch player worth leaning
  into\, this intimate listening room performance that he curated will make
  for an exceptional show. Ezra Holloway is a musician\, songwriter\, produ
 cer\, and frontman for the crunchy band Man Made Tragedies. He cut his tee
 th in Saxtons River\, building a reputation for his mix of rock\, pop\, pu
 nk\, and alternative style music with catchy melodies\, introspective lyri
 cs\, and energetic live shows. He's a college man these days. George Nostr
 and is a southern Vermont legend... a tireless performer\, local music pro
 moter\, writer\, and trouble-maker. He grew up in Bellows Falls and lives 
 in Rutland now. Nostrand offers an affably freewheeling musical stew\, sea
 soned with trans-generational and genre-hopping inspirations. An entertain
 er and storyteller\, he's at home on stages of all shapes and sizes. Stage
  33 Live is a casual and intimate industrial-rustic listening room in a fo
 rmer factory hosting local\, regional\, and national performances and pres
 entations of original material. No bar or kitchen\, the stage is the missi
 on\; coffee / soda / juice / water and weird snacks available by donation.
  More information about the nonprofit\, all-volunteer project\, and this a
 nd other upcoming events\, online at stage33live.com Stage 33 Live gratefu
 lly acknowledges the help of so many individuals without whom none of this
  would be able to happen\, and institutional support this season from The 
 Island Corporation\, WOOL-FM\, Guilford Sound\, and the Rockingham Arts & 
 Museum Project to help fund improvements and maintenance\, and generally s
 mooth out a lot of the rough edges. Stage 33 Live is a 501(c)3 nonprofit o
 rganization\, and all donations are deductible to the fullest extent. Volu
 nteers run the thing from stem to stern.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Stage 33 Live\, 33 Bridge Street\, Bellows Falls VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jesse-pete
 rs-ezra-holloway-and-george-nostrand-at-stage-33-live-15-11-2026-11-21-18
END:VEVENT
