BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kinhaven Semester Program Concert
DTSTART:20261122T160000
DTEND:20261122T173000
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:459be324f325f5614dc19ebcd2a63d@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Kinhaven\, located on a picturesque 31-acre campus in Weston\,
  VT\, celebrates its milestone 75th Anniversary in 2027\, as well as the s
 econd year of its Semester Program intensive for exceptional high school s
 tring students\, in collaboration with Burr and Burton Academy (BBA). The 
 first of its kind in the nation\, the Semester Program combines high-level
  academics at BBA with rigorous musical training at Kinhaven\, where stude
 nts live\, study\, and perform with each other and artistic faculty\, the 
 Trillium String Quartet\, with violinist and Co-Executive Director Deborah
  Buck. Semester Program Concerts are free and take place from September to
  December at venues across Vermont. At its core\, Kinhaven is about transf
 ormation. Since 1952\, Kinhaven has honored its mission of developing peop
 le through music by offering joyous and rigorous musical development and p
 erformance opportunities in a deeply collaborative environment\, without t
 echnology. For more information\, please visit: www.kinhaven.org.\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, 2 Cherry Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/kinhaven-s
 emester-program-concert-02-11-2026-19-18-49
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mandala Tea Light Class
DTSTART:20261122T110000
DTEND:20261122T140000
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:e5ed7609d4a635074965b28b8966f5@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Pub to to design and paint a decorative mandala
  on a tea-light holder. Mandala painting is a variation on a meditative ar
 t form that is over 2\,000 years old! You’ll use vibrant acrylic paints 
 and create a one-of-a kind object to add to your home decor. Designs can b
 e as simple or intricate as you imagine. Martha will instruct us in how to
  use dotting tools and teach the folk art style brush strokes used in the 
 Mandalas above. The harmony of the final piece comes from the relaxing rep
 etitive painting. Experience some colorful zen and leave your mess in the 
 Arts Department! Cost: FREE\, includes all materials! Thanks to a grant fr
 om the Vermont Community Fund! Limited Class Size\, BYOB\, snacks welcome!
  Please save your spot! You can stop in when the pub is open or email fran
 klinartsdepartment@gmail.com to reserve your seat. Meet your teacher — a
 rtist Martha Kinney. Martha is a native Vermonter who specializes in Early
  American Decoration and has taught classes ranging from barn quilts and c
 reative beading to traditional arts like vinegar grain painting and theore
 ms (stunning stenciled images on velvet). She is a guild member of the His
 torical Society of Early American Decoration and the Society of Decorative
  Painters and has been instructing and inspiring artists for three decades
  and counting!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Dick Wright Public House\, 5204 Main St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/mandala-te
 a-light-class-17-11-2026-13-08-39
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open House Art Exhibit
DTSTART:20261122T133000
DTEND:20261122T163000
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:5ac1a44db9a6d97b1663bae6a825ff@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Us for an Open House at McIndoes Academy Community Center
 ! Come explore the newly renovated buildings at McIndoes Academy Community
  Center in McIndoe Falls\, Vermont! Enjoy light refreshments\, take a guid
 ed tour\, and discover the history and character of this special community
  landmark. The open house will feature an art exhibit showcasing the works
  of William O. Wallace\, a local historical figure whose artwork offers a 
 glimpse into our area’s artistic and cultural heritage. Some pieces will
  be available for purchase\, while others will be on display for the durat
 ion of the event. We look forward to welcoming you!\n\nSources: Vermont Pu
 blic
LOCATION:McIndoes Academy Community Center\, 37 Academy Ln
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/open-house
 -art-exhibit-15-10-2026-15-21-10
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Sonny' Documentary Returns to Mountain Park Cinema
DTSTART:20261122T180000
DTEND:20261122T235900
DTSTAMP:20261122T183446Z
UID:0bbef7e63c2c71e8b16fc9ea087f78@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:After 3 sold out showings\, the documentary 'Sonny' returns to
  Mountain Park Cinema on November 22nd @ 6pm. Showings are free to public 
 with donations graciously accepted at the door. Donations will support the
  East Dover Fire Department\, Mountain Park Cinema and the filmmaker Matt 
 Oakes. We hope to see you there! Film Synopsis: A touching tribute to a lo
 cal legend\, Sonny is an intimate documentary that follows the life of Son
 ny Brown\, a 94-year-old farmer who has called East Dover home his entire 
 life. Throughout nearly a century of change\, Sonny has traded horses for 
 tractors and a crosscut saw for a chainsaw yet remained deeply rooted in t
 he land and the community that shaped him. At its heart\, Sonny celebrates
  a beloved husband\, father\, grandfather\, and great-grandfather whose un
 wavering work ethic and quiet devotion to others remind us that the greate
 st legacies are often built through a lifetime of quiet service. A true Ea
 st Dover story. For those who know Sonny\, this is an opportunity to see h
 is story through film. For those who don't\, it is a chance to learn about
  a remarkable local Vermont icon and a part of East Dover's history. The f
 ilm's music was scored by another local of the Deerfield Valley\, Logan Bo
 yd. Mountain Park Cinema Artist Group Info Matt Oakes mattoakesmedia@gmail
 .com https://www.firesidemediacompany.com/ Mountain Park Cinema 4 Mountain
  Park Plaza West Dover \, Vermont 05356 https://www.memhall.org/ Submit An
  Event Find out what's happening in your neck of the woods with Vermont Pu
 blic's free Events newsletter. Email Address * Editorial Emails Breaking N
 ews | sent occasionally The Frequency | Daily News Update\, sent weekday m
 ornings Capitol Recap | Vermont Legislature Wrap\, sent Fridays during the
  session Brave Little State | People-Powered Journalism\, sent every other
  Saturday But Why | A Podcast For Curious Kids\, sent every other Friday H
 omegoings | A righteous space for art and race\, sent bi-weekly following 
 an episode drop Out There | Out There | Your monthly dose of the environme
 nt + the great outdoors\, sent Thursday mor Supporter Emails Membership Re
 newal Notices | Sent 12 months after your most recent contribution The Pre
 sident's Report | A letter from our president exclusively for members of o
 ur Producers Circle The Transmitter | A behind-the-scenes newsletter exclu
 sively for active members\, sent the first Tues But Why Fan Club | Activit
 y Newsletter exclusively for active members of the But Why Fan Club\, sent
  Other Fundraising Emails | Matching challenges\, prize drawings and more
 \, sent periodically Audience Emails Program Schedules | Full TV listings 
 for all channels\, sent monthly This Week | Weekly program highlights\, se
